==============================================================================
ADVERSARIAL VERIFICATION SUMMARY (kind-pasteur, exact rationals)
==============================================================================
VERDICT on the "iterated-peel dichotomy" claim for OPEN-Q-108: HOLDS (as a
REDUCTION, not a full proof) -- exactly as the claim itself states.

CONFIRMED:
 - Margins mu_k = cap_k - Q(k-1) where Q(k-1)=plateau-MAX over bounded (k-1)-sets
   = Plat(consec_{k-1}) (consec IS the plateau argmax): mu_8..mu_12 =
   0.18486/0.13216/0.15651/0.19402/0.25490 (min mu_9). Matches claim EXACTLY.
 - (A) chain identity p0(E)=p0(core)+sum(1/7)p1(E_{i-1})+sum Delta_{w_i}: EXACT
   telescoping, 0/200 lhs!=rhs. PROVED.
 - (B) per-step comb bound |Delta_{w_i}|<=(6/49)V(E_{i-1})/w_i: 0 failures over
   2230 peel steps (worst ratio 0.26) + 0 over 8869 small-w + 0 over 20000
   single-far bounded-E' stress (worst 0.51). HOLDS (THM-546/547 PROVED).
 - (C) plateau telescope PlatTotal<=Q(k-1): 0/500 failures.
 - (D) V<=C*k is FALSE (max V/#elem=228); V=Theta(sigma), sup V/sigma~1.30-1.41;
   V<=7*sigma is a RIGOROUS majorant (0 failures). Matches claim.
 - SEPARATED branch: ChainB=sum(6/49)V/w drops below mu_9 at w1=50 for k=9
   two-far w2=2w1 (ChainB=0.12490<=0.13216); full UB=PlatTot+ChainB<=cap_9.
   Claim's "k=9 closes for w1>=50" is PRECISE.
 - BALANCED branch: ChainB EXPLODES (0.44/0.36/0.76 for k=10,11 clusters),
   does NOT beat mu_k -- iterated comb FAILS to close balanced, exactly as the
   claim admits. Actual p0 stays far below cap (the bound fails, not the truth).
 - HUNT: ZERO p0>cap over ~60000 wide primitive k-sets (k=8..12) across boundary
   span15-30, resonant gcd, multi-scale, near-pinned AP, random, plateau-adversary.
 - EXHAUSTIVE single-far collar consec_{k-1}+w (w in 15..200): 0 violations,
   thinnest margin +0.12143 at k=9 (consec_8 + 68). Binding case is the collar.

ENGINE BUG FOUND & FIXED (in THIS verification script only, not the claim's):
 - A fast re-implementation of analyze() had an early-exit `if len(hitcolors)==6:
   break`. Since hitcolors may include color 0 (outer sector), |hitcolors|==6 does
   NOT imply sectors 1..6 all hit -> under-counted hits -> WRONG (too-low) p0
   (consec_8 gave 13/70=0.186 instead of 481/1470=0.327). This SPURIOUSLY produced
   2 comb-bound "failures" and wrong margins (mu_9=0.253 instead of 0.132). After
   removing the break, engine matches the reference (prompt spec) 0/300 mismatch,
   and ALL anomalies vanish. The claim's own script uses the correct reference
   engine and was never affected.

SURVIVING GAP (the claim's honest residual, CONFIRMED real):
 The BALANCED far-cluster regime is NOT closed by iterated largest-first peel
 (V=Theta(sigma) => O(r) chain bound). Closure is DELEGATED to THM-531 dilation
 (far cluster = dilated bounded model) + the DONE finite span window. This is the
 SAME obstruction THM-548 sec.5 already named ("iterating leaves a wide base where
 V blows up; clusters need SIMULTANEOUS peel from the bounded base"). The iterated-
 peel angle therefore RE-DERIVES the separated closure and RE-DELEGATES the
 balanced case -- it introduces NO new analytic gap, but it does NOT itself close
 OPEN-Q-108. The one step that would make the SEPARATED branch fully rigorous
 (not just VERIFIED) is promoting V(E')<=c*sigma(E') from empirical c~1.3 to the
 rigorous V<=7*sigma (which only loosens the explicit rho cutoff).
